        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::bf857de4927d7e4425b19335",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "material_status"
          ],
          "value": "resolved",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::5295b27a17104b3c8d579065",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "approach"
          ],
          "value": "The authors conduct a narrative review of existing literature. They categorize host factors into four main domains: circulating immune compartment, germline genetics, phenotypic/external features, and gut microbiota. For each domain, they summarize key findings from clinical studies (retrospective analyses, post-hoc trial data, prospective cohorts) and preclinical models (murine studies). They discuss proposed biological mechanisms linking these factors to ICI efficacy, such as immune cell trafficking, antigen presentation, metabolic modulation, and innate immune priming. The review also notes discrepancies in findings across different studies and cancer types, emphasizing the need for validation.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::5ad79c8cd8f5e794f9d067b7",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "contribution_and_limits"
          ],
          "value": {
            "contribution": "Provides a comprehensive synthesis of host-based biomarker candidates beyond tumour tissue, categorizing them into immune, genetic, phenotypic, and microbial domains. Highlights the potential for modifiable factors (diet, microbiome, medications) as targets for combination therapies.",
            "limits": "As a narrative review, it does not present new primary data. Many associations described are based on retrospective analyses or small prospective cohorts, lacking robust validation in large-scale randomized trials. Findings show significant heterogeneity across cancer types and study methodologies, limiting immediate clinical applicability. The review explicitly states that these are candidate biomarkers requiring further validation."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::581d07e319b88eadf79d493d",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "key_findings"
          ],
          "value": {
            "conditions": "Circulating immune factors",
            "finding": "High baseline neutrophil-to-lymphocyte ratio (NLR) is associated with worse ICI outcomes; eosinophilia is linked to better outcomes. Specific T-cell receptor (TCR) diversity in peripheral PD1+ CD8+ T cells correlates with improved progression-free survival in NSCLC. High IL-8 levels negatively correlate with efficacy."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::cf4c93036684481a24b171e9",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "key_findings"
          ],
          "value": {
            "conditions": "Germline genetics",
            "finding": "HLA-A*03 allele association with poorer OS was not consistently replicated. HLA-I heterozygosity and evolutionary divergence generally associate with better outcomes, though effects vary by cancer type (e.g., HLA-B44 supertype has opposite effects in melanoma vs. NSCLC). FCGR3A V158F SNP associates with improved response to ipilimumab in melanoma."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::b3cfba2f8f859a528c563271",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "key_findings"
          ],
          "value": {
            "conditions": "Phenotypic and external features",
            "finding": "An 'obesity paradox' exists where higher BMI correlates with better ICI survival in some cancers, potentially mediated by leptin-induced PD1 expression on T cells. High cholesterol also correlates with better anti-PD1 outcomes. Gender effects are controversial. Corticosteroid use (for supportive care) negatively impacts ICI efficacy, while antihistamines may have a positive effect via histamine pathway modulation."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::066a2c2fbd5317027ece5054",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "key_findings"
          ],
          "value": {
            "conditions": "Gut microbiota",
            "finding": "Baseline gut microbiota composition and diversity influence ICI efficacy. Specific genera (e.g., Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) are often positively associated, while others (e.g., Bacteroides eggerthii) are negatively associated, though consensus is lacking due to methodological differences. Mechanisms include production of immunomodulatory metabolites (short-chain fatty acids, inosine), activation of innate immune receptors (NOD2, STING), and molecular mimicry between bacterial and tumour antigens."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::2dbc1a4d2e79a33875d890d5",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "paper_kind"
          ],
          "value": "review",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::031338a121dcefffb44b207b",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "problem_or_question"
          ],
          "value": "To address the unpredictability of tumour responses to ICIs and the limitations of current tumour-centric biomarkers (such as PD-L1, TMB, and MMR deficiency) which require invasive tissue sampling and lack cross-cancer generalizability. The review aims to identify and evaluate host-based factors that could offer better pre-treatment prediction of ICI benefit.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::3c83913156da7e0539bfa5a2",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "research_scope"
          ],
          "value": "The review focuses on host factors influencing the response of patients with solid tumours to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It covers circulating immune compartments, germline genetic features, phenotypic and external features (exposome), and gut microbial features.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::82cc9e6fd19a61ef6fee2b48",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "work_summary"
          ],
          "value": "This review article synthesizes emerging evidence regarding non-tumour-centric host factors that may serve as predictive biomarkers for ICI efficacy. The authors argue that current FDA-approved biomarkers are limited by their reliance on tumour tissue and poor generalizability across cancer types. Consequently, they explore alternative host-based predictors, including peripheral blood immune markers (e.g., neutrophil-to-lymphocyte ratio, eosinophils, TCR repertoire), germline genetics (e.g., HLA alleles, Fc-gamma receptor polymorphisms), phenotypic traits (e.g., obesity, cholesterol, gender), exogenous factors (e.g., medications like corticosteroids or antibiotics, diet), and specifically the gut microbiota. The paper highlights the potential modifiability of several factors, suggesting avenues for co-therapies to enhance ICI therapeutic index.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::c424b1ec5f22edc8c8467b99",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "broader_review_uses"
          ],
          "value": {
            "material": "Summaries of circulating immune markers (NLR, eosinophils), germline genetics (HLA, FCGR3A), and phenotypic factors (obesity, cholesterol, gender) and their associations with ICI efficacy."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::fb182cc527a1e60a9482d1ba",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "broader_review_uses"
          ],
          "value": {
            "material": "Evidence that corticosteroids, antibiotics, diet (fibre), and specific medications (antihistamines, beta-blockers) can modulate ICI efficacy, partly through microbiome or immune pathways."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::f7d6c0e58b444106855fe1ce",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "broader_review_uses"
          ],
          "value": {
            "material": "Discussion of discrepancies in microbiome findings due to differences in stool collection, DNA extraction, sequencing methods (16S vs. shotgun), and bioinformatic pipelines."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::f6d31f17449d65516fa7cb1b",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions"
          ],
          "value": {
            "boundaries": "Associations are observational and inconsistent across studies. The review emphasizes that these are correlations, not proven causal relationships for all contexts. Clinical endpoints vary (ORR, PFS, OS).",
            "contribution": "Lists specific gut bacterial species and genera (e.g., Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium spp., Bacteroides eggerthii) that have been associated with positive or negative ICI outcomes in various solid tumour cohorts. Notes the lack of consensus and potential reasons for discrepancies (methodology, geography, cancer type).",
            "facet_id": "F1"
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::f5ce6fafc64a7c4165ef38dc",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions"
          ],
          "value": {
            "boundaries": "Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or small human subsets. The review notes that the relative contribution of each mechanism in humans is still being elucidated. Some mechanisms (like butyrate's effect) can be context-dependent (positive for anti-PD1, negative for anti-CTLA4).",
            "contribution": "Details proposed mechanisms by which gut microbiota influence ICI efficacy: 1) Production of immunomodulatory metabolites (butyrate, inosine, hippurate); 2) Activation of innate immune receptors (NOD2, STING, TLRs) leading to myeloid cell priming and type I interferon production; 3) Molecular mimicry between bacterial epitopes and tumour neoantigens leading to cross-reactive T cells.",
            "facet_id": "F2"
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::b043611ba77b73bd423db17a",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions"
          ],
          "value": "The review covers multiple cancer types (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, etc.), so findings should not be assumed to apply uniformly to all solid tumours without checking specific context.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::ec17513be6040007b4b17183",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions"
          ],
          "value": "Microbial associations are highly variable; the review explicitly states there is little consensus on specific species, so any single species mentioned should be treated as a candidate rather than a definitive marker.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::6aa91e78c58f0ef496634db8",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions"
          ],
          "value": "Mechanisms described are largely hypothetical or based on preclinical models; causal links in humans are not fully established.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0269"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::f620f751523a363ce2cf08ee",
          "source_handle": "P0269",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions"
          ],
          "value": "The review is a narrative summary, not a systematic meta-analysis; it does not provide pooled effect sizes or rigorous statistical comparisons.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
